 "fieldNotes": "Did this ride start or end at home? If so, it can only be told as a views-only story with no track, route or distances.\nThe track I just added should be cut off after 7 miles as the trip home was recorded by mistake.\n\nPrivacy first: the recording ran on into the trip home. Did the ride also start at home? If so, it can only be told views-only, with no track, map, route or distances. Either way, nothing about the trip home goes in the text.\nNo it did not start at home. Started a few minutes into the trail.\n\nThe current figures (7.8 miles, 1 h 2 m moving and so on) still include the trip home. Can you re-trim the track at 7 miles and send the new figures before any numbers go in?\nyes\n\nWas the trip home recorded while driving or while riding? It matters for whether the 'forgot to stop the tracker' gag fits.\nDriving a car and forgot.\n\nWho is in the hammock, and are they OK appearing in the photo? Should they be named or stay anonymous?\nMy wife. Yes\n\nWhere was this? Trailhead or public-land name, and which lake?\nFlume Trail near Incline Village.\n\nAnything from the ride itself to add: route, who came along, whether Marley was there?\nMarley, Helena and Myself.\n\nPlease send the re-trimmed figures (cut at 7 miles). The current ones still include the drive, so no numbers are in the text yet.\nSorry my mistake that was for the last ride. This one is perfect.\n\nYou mentioned Helena. The show guide keeps your wife unnamed, so the draft says \"my wife\". Do you want her named from now on? If so, the guide and her consent entry need updating.\nYes that works.\n\nThe draft says Lake Tahoe, since the Flume Trail near Incline Village looks over it. Is that right?\nCorrect\n\nMarley isn't visible in the photo. Do you have a photo of Marley from this ride, or anything Marley did on the trail worth adding?\nShe is in the videos I think. That is ok.\n\nHelena is now named in the text: please update her consent entry and the show guide's cast line (wife, named Helena) before publishing.\nNo. Should be \"My wife\".\n\nSince the trip-home recording belonged to the last ride, I took out the 'forgot to stop the tracker' line here. OK to leave it out?\nyes",
 "post": {
  "title": "A hammock above the lake",
  "body": "On the last day of August 2024 I rode the Flume Trail near Incline Village. Marley and my wife came along. We set out around half past nine, and at 11:25 in the morning we had stopped in the pines above Lake Tahoe.\n\nThe hammock went up between two trees on a slope of pine needles and dry ground. Big granite boulders sat in the low green brush, and through the trunks you could see the lake, deep blue, with mountains on the far side. The sky was clear apart from a few thin clouds.\n\nMy wife was in the hammock. I was the one taking the picture.\n\nThe ride came to about eight miles, with only a couple hundred feet of climbing and about an hour of it spent moving. We were out a bit over three hours in all."
 },
 "episode": {
  "title": "The hammock stop",
  "script": "Late morning, the last day of August, in the pines above Lake Tahoe.\n\nChristian was out on the Flume Trail near Incline Village, with his wife and Marley along. They set out around half past nine. At twenty-five past eleven, the ride had turned into a stop.\n\nA blue hammock hung between two trees. Granite boulders sat in the brush below it, and through the trunks the lake showed up deep blue, with mountains on the far shore.\n\n***\n\nHis wife was in the hammock. Christian was behind the camera, which is its own kind of rest.\n\nBy the track, the ride came to about eight miles and only a couple hundred feet of climbing, about an hour of it spent moving. The whole outing ran a bit over three hours. Some of the rest went to the hammock.",
  "audio": "data/audio/2024-08-31-a-hammock-above-the-lake.mp3"
 },
